{
  "dom_id": "step-206315",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Calculating the Average Rate of Change of a Function",
  "problem": "A curve is defined as $y = 2x^2.$ Find the average rate of change of $y$ over the interval $[0,5].$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=2x^2.$ Applying the formula for the average rate of change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(0)}{5-(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2(5)^{2})-(2(0)^{2})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{50}{5} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
